      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name} Its been happening off and on since the chatbox was introduced and I run into it a couple times a week, but I don't know exactly what triggers it. So yes and no.\n\nThe only details I'm certain of are that this occurs because an invisible Quick Menu appears on top of the chatbox keyboard, and that it remains this way until you rejoin the world. I've also never experienced this in desktop mode.\n\nTo help eliminate as many variables as possible here are some extra details for my case:\n\n- I use the A button on my left Index controller to open the chatbox.\n\n- I have the 'responsive menus' setting enabled and my MM/chatbox windows are 'unlocked'.\n\n- I don't have the best PC so low framerates might be involved, my lowest average is ~20.\n\n- I only ever notice this issue pop up after a couple dozen messages have been sent. As far as I know this is caused by interacting with it and doesn't start occurring on its own upon joining a world.\n\n- I often 'interrupt' the Main Menu and Quick Menu using my chatbox button to close them, this may have something to do with it, but I haven't been able to induce it this way manually so I'm not sure.\n\nHope that helps. I'll try to remember to grab a recording of the issue next time I run into it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
