      "mergedPostDetails": "This bug is a tricky tough one to reproduce and to explain, so i've recorded a video in one of the moments that it happened. I can't reproduce it, i only know that it happens 1 out of 30 times i open my vrc keyboard to type.\n\nThe issue is, i open the keyboard to type in my chatbox, and there are certain keys that i can't click on, they don't highligh when i hover my laser over it, then i find out at the bottom right that it says messages like: \n\n- Discover and visit new worlds\n\n- Change your avatar\n\n- Browse users in the instance and your friends\n\n- Etc...\n\nThose are messages that you can read when you hover the laser in your quick menu's options.\n\nAgain, i can't reproduce this, but it happens, it happens to me more than once every day. Just open my keyboard and start typing and i can't click on  Send because it thinks there is another menu above the keyboard (quick menu stuck in front of it). In the video i found out that i can dodge that invisible menu by using playspace mover so i can click on those inputs that were blocked by it.\n\nPlease, watch all the video to try to understand what is happening, and sorry for the bottom right mirrored view.\n\nhttps://streamable.com/d1u824\n\nI use Index headset and index controllers, in case its necessary to know, and this has been happening since 2~ months ago.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Keyboard's inputs get blocked by a static invisible Quick Menu",
